From a35487a6d602f534a3047b8f46ea18217cba1f1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:52:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browser): open and close background tabs in the bound
 window

Agents could only act in tabs that already existed, so working on a page
meant navigating the user's current tab away.

browser_open_tab {target_id, url} opens a tab with Target.createTarget
background:true, which Chromium adds unselected to the profile's most
recently active window without activating it. The tool proves the tab
landed in the bound window (else closes it again and refuses), adds it to
the binding's tab table and returns its tab_id. browser_close_tab
{target_id, tab_id} closes only tabs the same session opened.

The window-level proof reuses the tab revalidation chain (now split into
revalidate_record), both tools sit behind the browser_bound_input adapter
like the other page mutations, and the existing-profile CDP policy admits
Target.createTarget and Target.closeTarget for them.
