+### Background tabs
+
+`browser_open_tab` opens a tab in the bound window without selecting it or
+activating the window, and returns its `tab_id` in the same binding, so work
+can happen beside the user's current page instead of navigating it away. Only
+`http:`, `https:`, and `about:` URLs are accepted. Chromium adds background tabs
+to the profile's most recently active window; if that isn't the bound window,
+the driver closes the tab again and refuses with
+`browser_wrong_target_refused`. `browser_close_tab` closes only tabs the same
+session opened this way and refuses every other tab.
+
+```text
+browser_open_tab
+  '{"target_id":"<target>","url":"https://example.com",
+    "session":"browser-run-1"}'
+browser_close_tab
+  '{"target_id":"<target>","tab_id":"<new tab>","session":"browser-run-1"}'
+```
+
 ### JavaScript dialogs
 
 `browser_dialog` handles only page-owned `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, and
